+# Hostile gate review: K=16 screened cofinal family
+
+Target claim: `screened-census-grok46-20260903.md` Sec.6.2 / AUDIT delta
+17(v).  Frozen inputs were verified first against the requested SHA-256 list.
+No ledger edits; no `jc2-lean`; no ideation-lane reports were read.
+
+Driver added for this lane:
+
+```text
+box/k16gate-drivers-20260903/k16_gate.py
+```
+
+Commands run:
+
+```text
+sha256sum -c <requested list>                         # exit 0
+python3 box/k16gate-drivers-20260903/k16_gate.py      # exit 0
+python3 box/descentradii-drivers-20260903/phi_delta.py # exit 0
+```
+
+The K16 harness loads the frozen Moh enumerator and frozen whole-tree drivers
+from `/tmp/jc2-lane.d5sry1/inputs`.  For nested-pack it uses the repo
+`box/branch-orbits-v2-20260903` directory only for its required
+`knapsack_v2.py`; the nested-pack file itself matches the frozen hash.
+
+## Verdicts
+
+| item | verdict | scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| (1) symbolic path arithmetic `(1)-(13)` | CONFIRMED | all integer `t >= 1` |
+| (2) `moh_skeleton_full.py` census samples | CONFIRMED | measured at `t=1,2,3,5,8` |
+| (3) gap-free whole-tree screens | CONFIRMED | symbolic witness, measured at `t=1,2,3,5,8` in both drivers |
+| (4) exact nested-pack DP | CONFIRMED | all `t >= 1`; measured samples agree |
+| (5) Prop.6.3 descent datum and Phi radii | CONFIRMED | all `t >= 1`; p.207 control at `t=1` matches |
+| (6) cofinality consequence | CONFIRMED | gap-free for this family |
+
+Consequence: `Q3(f)` after the screen is **NO**.  The screened census is
+cofinally nonempty via the K16 ray.
+
+## Hash Gate
+
+Every frozen input matched exactly:
+
+```text
+29a6f54dff3dbe2e2ad4cbb07dfdb7b18168e86848d5abb4644f2024f766b82d  screened-census-grok46-20260903.md
+b28e6b3d36c2a6907b4175fb914e29757c5eec3b8a4a82bea3099dc88b6853cf  screened_census.py
+27551a88ab6ee9f62a5606010adcd9d4a1fd4411a09d97c699e13a67c84f7096  whole-tree-review-opus5-20260903.md
+4402bf528d18f8c409935433ce7a0bea5e3b2e6c23a1735f4341218035d11ad9  opus5_probe.py
+875c098a2a9465e146c77757e3d197be8af35f46ee4e772321acf8ca33b5fef8  full_tree_partition.py
+36b374b21b3768e841ad2cc2168d7e669d9b0d6e6b6c8d1737d203acbd079067  nested_pack.py
+fb137b92d88b2f59f369bbffb2a0591aed69e9294135751c329da9eea58f6948  census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md
+d20bf0841a1ba2b229d423bb948e6c4474a4f5a83f55148071cae39cb6c506c2  moh_skeleton_full.py
+4bcb512d47cf9f935c6a2c0c7b8251ae16b3e4f73b4794abbef2d1702846c7c1  phi_delta.py
+```
+
+Repo copies used for direct execution also match the charged script hashes for
+`box/moh_skeleton_full.py`, both whole-tree `full_tree_partition.py` copies,
+`box/wholetree-drivers-20260903/opus5_probe.py`,
+`box/branch-orbits-v2-20260903/nested_pack.py`, and
+`box/descentradii-drivers-20260903/phi_delta.py`.
+
+## 1. Symbolic Algebra in `t`
+
+Set
+
+```text
+e = 3t + 1,  d = 2t + 1,  t >= 1
+n = 16e = 48t + 16
+m = 16d = 32t + 16
+M1 = -m,  M2 = n - 12 = 48t + 4,  M3 = n - 2 = 48t + 14
+V2 = V3 = 3,  V4 = d4 = 2,  s = 3
+```
+
+The integer coprimality is not just polynomial-gcd: `3d - 2e = 1`, hence
+`gcd(e,d)=1` for every integer `t`.  Therefore `d2=gcd(n,m)=16`.
+
+The next gcds are exact:
+
+```text
+M2 = 4(12t + 1), with 12t+1 odd, so d3 = gcd(16,M2) = 4.
+M3 = 2(24t + 7), with 24t+7 odd, so d4 = gcd(4,M3) = 2.
+```
+
+So the gcd ladder is exactly
+
+```text
+(d1,d2,d3,d4) = (n,16,4,2).
+```
+
+The windows from Def.5.1(2) are constant:
+
+```text
+i=3:  d3/(n-M3) = 4/2 = 2      and V4*d3/d4 = 2*4/2 = 4
+      hence 2 < V3=3 <= 4.
+
+i=2:  d2/(n-M2) = 16/12 = 4/3  and V3*d2/d3 = 3*16/4 = 12
+      hence 4/3 < V2=3 <= 12.
+```
+
+Def.5.1(3), using the printed formula recorded in `census-rebase`, gives:
+
+```text
+delta3 = 1 - (n-M3)/(n-M3-1) = 1 - 2/1 = -1.
+
+delta2 = 1 - 12*(3*2-4)/(3*12-4)
+       = 1 - 12*2/32
+       = 1/4.
+
+delta1 = (7t + 2)/(4(3t + 1)).
+```
+
+For `j=2`, `L2=1`, hence `A2=den(delta2)=4`.  With the notation of the
+charged claim:
+
+```text
+P = V3*d2/d3       = 3*16/4 = 12
+Q = V3*(n-M2)/d3   = 3*12/4 = 9
+P = 3*A2 + 0
+triangle = 3, square = 0
+```
+
+Thus `P == 0 mod A2`, so the minimum fixed-zero multiplicity is `b=0`; there
+is no forced major zero.  Moh (10) holds because `V2=3 <= triangle=3`.
+Moh (11) fails because `V2-square = 3` is not `0 mod 4`.  This is exactly
+the `(10)`-only case.
+
+For `j=1`, `L1=lcm(den(delta3),den(delta2))=4`, so
+
+```text
+L1*delta1 = (7t+2)/(3t+1).
+```
+
+The numerator and denominator are coprime for all integers `t`, since
+`3(7t+2) - 7(3t+1) = -1`.  Therefore
+
+```text
+A1 = 3t + 1 = e.
+```
+
+Bottom condition (12) is an identity:
+
+```text
+e*V2 = 3e                         == 0 mod A1
+d*V2 - 1 = 3(2t+1)-1 = 6t+2 = 2e  == 0 mod A1.
+```
+
+Bottom condition (13) is false for `t >= 1`:
+
+```text
+d*V2 = 6t+3 = 2e+1    == 1  mod A1
+e*V2 - 1 = 3e-1       == -1 mod A1.
+```
+
+The D1 contribution is
+
+```text
+q = (1-delta1)*d*e/(d+e) = (2t+1)/4.
+```
+
+The nonzero orbit size is `|O|=A2=4`, so the single bottom packet has weight
+
+```text
+w = |O|*V2 = 4*3 = 12.
+```
+
+The local budget used by nested-pack is
+
+```text
+u = V3*K/d3 = 3*16/4 = 12.
+```
+
+Thus one packet exactly fills the parent:
+
+```text
+N = |O|*V2*q = 12q = 3(2t+1) = 6t+3.
+```
+
+Conclusion for item (1): Moh `(1)-(13)` hold symbolically for every integer
+`t >= 1`, not merely for the measured samples.
+
+## 2. Census Emission Samples
+
+I ran the frozen `moh_skeleton_full.py` census through the K16 harness at the
+requested values.  Each degree contains exactly one row with
+`m=32t+16`, `M=[n-12,n-2]`, `V={2:3,3:3}`, and that row has
+`windows_ok=True` and `full_ok=True`.
+
+| `t` | `n` | row count | `A1` | `q` | `N` | exact group `V2` values |
+|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| 1 | 64 | 1 | 4 | 3/4 | 9 | `[3]` |
+| 2 | 112 | 1 | 7 | 5/4 | 15 | `[3]` |
+| 3 | 160 | 1 | 10 | 7/4 | 21 | `[3]` |
+| 5 | 256 | 1 | 16 | 11/4 | 33 | `[3]` |
+| 8 | 400 | 1 | 25 | 17/4 | 51 | `[3]` |
+
+The requested measured census check is therefore CONFIRMED.  The symbolic
+loop conditions also show why this emits for all `t >= 1`: `K=16 <= n/3`,
+`d=2t+1` lies in `2 <= d < e`, `gcd(d,e)=1`, divisor chain `[4]` gives
+`s=3`, `gcd(16,M2)=4`, and the unique full bottom assignment in this exact
+group is `V2=3`.
+
+## 3. Whole-Tree Screens
+
+I checked the requested gap-free screen family with `opus5_probe.py`:
+
+```text
+partition-only, no Prop.5.6 danger       True
+partition + ODE, no Prop.5.6 danger      True
+gated Prop.5.6                           True
+gated Prop.5.6 + ODE                      True
+```
+
+For cross-check, the frozen `full_tree_partition.py` also accepts the selected
+path under its charged screens:
+
+```text
+C_FULL_TREE                              True
+C_FULL_TREE_ODE                          True
+```
+
+This was measured at every requested sample `t=1,2,3,5,8`.  The witness is
+independent of `t` except for the bottom `A1`.
+
+At the only tree level, `j=2`, the partition witness is:
+
+```text
+delta2 = 1/4
+A = 4
+P = 12
+Q = 9
+major threshold = d2/(n-M2) = 4/3
+fixed-zero multiplicity b = 0
+selected mode = nonzero
+selected multiplicity = V2 = 3
+nonzero p-orbit multiplicities = [3]
+```
+
+The sibling inventory is exact:
+
+```text
+q-root slots: 1 fixed zero root + (Q-1)/A = 2 nonzero A-orbits.
+
+fixed zero root:
+  p-multiplicity b=0, so it is not a p-factor and carries no lower major tree.
+
+selected nonzero orbit:
+  size A=4, p-multiplicity 3 at each conjugate root.
+  It is major because 3 > 4/3.
+  Each conjugate has the same bottom data:
+    A1=3t+1, condition (12)=true, condition (13)=false.
+
+unused nonzero q-orbit:
+  p-multiplicity 0, so it is an unused q-slot and carries no p-root child.
+```
+
+ODE nondegeneracy is also uniform:
+
+```text
+selected orbit: P - Q*3 = 12 - 27 = -15 != 0.
+fixed zero root: b=0, so the positive-zero-root ODE exclusion is not triggered.
+unused q-orbit: p-multiplicity 0 gives P - Q*0 = 12 != 0.
+```
+
+The Prop.5.6 danger flag is cleared by the selected nonzero label before the
+bottom.  Therefore this family does not consume the gapped ungated
+zero-chain use of Prop.5.6.  Survival is gap-free under the repaired/gated
+screen and also survives the stronger charged implementation.
+
+## 4. Nested-Pack DP
+
+The exact group has only the selected `V2=3` assignment in every requested
+census sample.  Nested-pack is exact at `s=3`; its debug helper labels the
+p-degree as `Q_of=12`, which is the same quantity called `P=12` above.
+
+The packet is:
+
+```text
+orbit size |O| = 4
+packet weight w = |O|*V2 = 12
+parent budget u = 12
+packet value c = |O|*V2*q = 6t+3
+```
+
+Therefore the DP has exactly one positive reachable integer:
+
+```text
+Nset = {6t+3}.
+```
+
+Measured nested-pack outputs:
+
+| `t` | `n` | DP integer set | cap |
+|---:|---:|---|---|
+| 1 | 64 | `{9}` | false |
+| 2 | 112 | `{15}` | false |
+| 3 | 160 | `{21}` | false |
+| 5 | 256 | `{33}` | false |
+| 8 | 400 | `{51}` | false |
+
+This confirms the exact nested packing claim.  The family is cofinal for
+`N >= 6`; it lies inside the finite campaign window `[6,16]` only at
+`t=1,2`.
+
+## 5. Prop.6.3 Descent
+
+Keep separate the two `u` quantities:
+
+```text
+nested-pack budget: u = V3*K/d3 = 12.
+Prop.6.3 top complement: u_s = d_s - V_s = d3 - V3 = 4 - 3 = 1.
+```
+
+Since `u_s=1`, the charged Prop.6.4 automatic hypothesis is met for every
+member of the ray.  The Jacobian exponent is
+
+```text
+v_s - u_s - 1 = 3 - 1 - 1 = 1,
+```
+
+so the descended monomial-Jacobian ray has `J ~ gamma`.
+
+The descended data are:
+
+```text
+n'  = n/d_s  = (48t+16)/4 = 12t+4 = 4(3t+1)
+m'  = m/d_s  = (32t+16)/4 = 8t+4  = 4(2t+1)
+M2' = M2/d_s = (48t+4)/4  = 12t+1
+V2' = 3
+k   = 1
+s'  = 2
+d'  = (d1',d2',d3') = (4(3t+1),4,1)
+```
+
+At `t=1`, this gives
+
+```text
+(n',m',M2',V2',k) = (16,12,13,3,1),
+```
+
+matching Moh p.207's `(16,12; 13; 3; X)` row to the datum.  The independent
+`phi_delta.py` control also prints:
+
+```text
+(16,12) from (64,48): raw=(-1/2, 1/8), Phi=(-1, 1/4),
+printed=(-1, 1/4), MATCH.
+```
+
+For general `t`, Def.5.1(3) on the descended `s'=2` data gives raw radii:
+
+```text
+raw delta2 = -1/2
+raw delta1 = t/(2(3t+1)).
+```
+
+By the Phi rule in the charged helper, `delta' = (k+1)*raw` and `k=1`, hence
+
+```text
+Phi delta2' = -1
+Phi delta1' = t/(3t+1).
+```
+
+The descent anchor does not vanish:
+
+```text
+n' - M2' - 1 = (12t+4) - (12t+1) - 1 = 2.
+```
+
+So `OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]` is closed negatively for this ray: the anchor is
+exactly `2` for all `t >= 1`.
+
+## OPEN Accounting
+
+`OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]` was the only OPEN directly created by this claim.
+
+Bounded quantity:
+
+```text
+n' - M'_{s'} - 1
+```
+
+Cheapest test:
+
+```text
+SymPy simplify((12*t+4) - (12*t+1) - 1) = 2.
+```
+
+Result: no vanishing on the K16 ray.  No new exit-price assertion is made in
+this report, so the `charge_basis=...` line from `FALLACY-v2.md` is not
+applicable.
+
+## Final Consequence
+
+The K16 family is not a measured accident.  The Moh `(1)-(13)` arithmetic is
+symbolic in `t`, the whole-tree witness is a nonzero orbit and therefore does
+not rely on the gapped ungated Prop.5.6 zero-chain step, ODE nondegeneracy is
+`12-27 != 0`, nested-pack gives exactly `{6t+3}`, and Prop.6.3/6.4 descends
+the ray to monomial-Jacobian degree pairs
+
+```text
+(n',m'; gamma) = (12t+4, 8t+4; gamma),  t >= 1.
+```
+
+Verdict: **CONFIRMED**.  The family's cofinality is gap-free.  Therefore the
+screened census is cofinally nonempty, and the claimed consequence is typed:
+
+```text
+Q3(f) after the screen is NO.
+```
+
