+## 1. Symbolic Algebra in `t`
+
+Set
+
+```text
+e = 3t + 1,  d = 2t + 1,  t >= 1
+n = 16e = 48t + 16
+m = 16d = 32t + 16
+M1 = -m,  M2 = n - 12 = 48t + 4,  M3 = n - 2 = 48t + 14
+V2 = V3 = 3,  V4 = d4 = 2,  s = 3
+```
+
+The integer coprimality is not just polynomial-gcd: `3d - 2e = 1`, hence
+`gcd(e,d)=1` for every integer `t`.  Therefore `d2=gcd(n,m)=16`.
+
+The next gcds are exact:
+
+```text
+M2 = 4(12t + 1), with 12t+1 odd, so d3 = gcd(16,M2) = 4.
+M3 = 2(24t + 7), with 24t+7 odd, so d4 = gcd(4,M3) = 2.
+```
+
+So the gcd ladder is exactly
+
+```text
+(d1,d2,d3,d4) = (n,16,4,2).
+```
+
+The windows from Def.5.1(2) are constant:
+
+```text
+i=3:  d3/(n-M3) = 4/2 = 2      and V4*d3/d4 = 2*4/2 = 4
+      hence 2 < V3=3 <= 4.
+
+i=2:  d2/(n-M2) = 16/12 = 4/3  and V3*d2/d3 = 3*16/4 = 12
+      hence 4/3 < V2=3 <= 12.
+```
+
+Def.5.1(3), using the printed formula recorded in `census-rebase`, gives:
+
+```text
+delta3 = 1 - (n-M3)/(n-M3-1) = 1 - 2/1 = -1.
+
+delta2 = 1 - 12*(3*2-4)/(3*12-4)
+       = 1 - 12*2/32
+       = 1/4.
+
+delta1 = (7t + 2)/(4(3t + 1)).
+```
+
+For `j=2`, `L2=1`, hence `A2=den(delta2)=4`.  With the notation of the
+charged claim:
+
+```text
+P = V3*d2/d3       = 3*16/4 = 12
+Q = V3*(n-M2)/d3   = 3*12/4 = 9
+P = 3*A2 + 0
+triangle = 3, square = 0
+```
+
+Thus `P == 0 mod A2`, so the minimum fixed-zero multiplicity is `b=0`; there
+is no forced major zero.  Moh (10) holds because `V2=3 <= triangle=3`.
+Moh (11) fails because `V2-square = 3` is not `0 mod 4`.  This is exactly
+the `(10)`-only case.
+
+For `j=1`, `L1=lcm(den(delta3),den(delta2))=4`, so
+
+```text
+L1*delta1 = (7t+2)/(3t+1).
+```
+
+The numerator and denominator are coprime for all integers `t`, since
+`3(7t+2) - 7(3t+1) = -1`.  Therefore
+
+```text
+A1 = 3t + 1 = e.
+```
+
+Bottom condition (12) is an identity:
+
+```text
+e*V2 = 3e                         == 0 mod A1
+d*V2 - 1 = 3(2t+1)-1 = 6t+2 = 2e  == 0 mod A1.
+```
+
+Bottom condition (13) is false for `t >= 1`:
+
+```text
+d*V2 = 6t+3 = 2e+1    == 1  mod A1
+e*V2 - 1 = 3e-1       == -1 mod A1.
+```
+
+The D1 contribution is
+
+```text
+q = (1-delta1)*d*e/(d+e) = (2t+1)/4.
+```
+
+The nonzero orbit size is `|O|=A2=4`, so the single bottom packet has weight
+
+```text
+w = |O|*V2 = 4*3 = 12.
+```
+
+The local budget used by nested-pack is
+
+```text
+u = V3*K/d3 = 3*16/4 = 12.
+```
+
+Thus one packet exactly fills the parent:
+
+```text
+N = |O|*V2*q = 12q = 3(2t+1) = 6t+3.
+```
+
+Conclusion for item (1): Moh `(1)-(13)` hold symbolically for every integer
+`t >= 1`, not merely for the measured samples.
+
+## 2. Census Emission Samples
+
+I ran the frozen `moh_skeleton_full.py` census through the K16 harness at the
