+# Hostile gate review: K=16 screened cofinal family
+
+Target claim: `screened-census-grok46-20260903.md` Sec.6.2 / AUDIT delta
+17(v).  Frozen inputs were verified first against the requested SHA-256 list.
+No ledger edits; no `jc2-lean`; no ideation-lane reports were read.
+
+Driver added for this lane:
+
+```text
+box/k16gate-drivers-20260903/k16_gate.py
+```
+
+Commands run:
+
+```text
+sha256sum -c <requested list>                         # exit 0
+python3 box/k16gate-drivers-20260903/k16_gate.py      # exit 0
+python3 box/descentradii-drivers-20260903/phi_delta.py # exit 0
+```
+
+The K16 harness loads the frozen Moh enumerator and frozen whole-tree drivers
+from `/tmp/jc2-lane.d5sry1/inputs`.  For nested-pack it uses the repo
+`box/branch-orbits-v2-20260903` directory only for its required
+`knapsack_v2.py`; the nested-pack file itself matches the frozen hash.
+
+## Verdicts
+
+| item | verdict | scope |
+|---|---|---|
+| (1) symbolic path arithmetic `(1)-(13)` | CONFIRMED | all integer `t >= 1` |
+| (2) `moh_skeleton_full.py` census samples | CONFIRMED | measured at `t=1,2,3,5,8` |
+| (3) gap-free whole-tree screens | CONFIRMED | symbolic witness, measured at `t=1,2,3,5,8` in both drivers |
+| (4) exact nested-pack DP | CONFIRMED | all `t >= 1`; measured samples agree |
+| (5) Prop.6.3 descent datum and Phi radii | CONFIRMED | all `t >= 1`; p.207 control at `t=1` matches |
+| (6) cofinality consequence | CONFIRMED | gap-free for this family |
+
+Consequence: `Q3(f)` after the screen is **NO**.  The screened census is
+cofinally nonempty via the K16 ray.
+
+## Hash Gate
+
+Every frozen input matched exactly:
+
+```text
+29a6f54dff3dbe2e2ad4cbb07dfdb7b18168e86848d5abb4644f2024f766b82d  screened-census-grok46-20260903.md
+b28e6b3d36c2a6907b4175fb914e29757c5eec3b8a4a82bea3099dc88b6853cf  screened_census.py
+27551a88ab6ee9f62a5606010adcd9d4a1fd4411a09d97c699e13a67c84f7096  whole-tree-review-opus5-20260903.md
+4402bf528d18f8c409935433ce7a0bea5e3b2e6c23a1735f4341218035d11ad9  opus5_probe.py
+875c098a2a9465e146c77757e3d197be8af35f46ee4e772321acf8ca33b5fef8  full_tree_partition.py
+36b374b21b3768e841ad2cc2168d7e669d9b0d6e6b6c8d1737d203acbd079067  nested_pack.py
+fb137b92d88b2f59f369bbffb2a0591aed69e9294135751c329da9eea58f6948  census-rebase-opus5-20260902.md
+d20bf0841a1ba2b229d423bb948e6c4474a4f5a83f55148071cae39cb6c506c2  moh_skeleton_full.py
+4bcb512d47cf9f935c6a2c0c7b8251ae16b3e4f73b4794abbef2d1702846c7c1  phi_delta.py
+```
+
+Repo copies used for direct execution also match the charged script hashes for
+`box/moh_skeleton_full.py`, both whole-tree `full_tree_partition.py` copies,
+`box/wholetree-drivers-20260903/opus5_probe.py`,
+`box/branch-orbits-v2-20260903/nested_pack.py`, and
+`box/descentradii-drivers-20260903/phi_delta.py`.
+
+## 1. Symbolic Algebra in `t`
+
+Set
+
+```text
+e = 3t + 1,  d = 2t + 1,  t >= 1
+n = 16e = 48t + 16
+m = 16d = 32t + 16
+M1 = -m,  M2 = n - 12 = 48t + 4,  M3 = n - 2 = 48t + 14
+V2 = V3 = 3,  V4 = d4 = 2,  s = 3
+```
+
+The integer coprimality is not just polynomial-gcd: `3d - 2e = 1`, hence
+`gcd(e,d)=1` for every integer `t`.  Therefore `d2=gcd(n,m)=16`.
+
+The next gcds are exact:
+
+```text
+M2 = 4(12t + 1), with 12t+1 odd, so d3 = gcd(16,M2) = 4.
+M3 = 2(24t + 7), with 24t+7 odd, so d4 = gcd(4,M3) = 2.
+```
+
+So the gcd ladder is exactly
+
+```text
+(d1,d2,d3,d4) = (n,16,4,2).
+```
+
+The windows from Def.5.1(2) are constant:
+
+```text
+i=3:  d3/(n-M3) = 4/2 = 2      and V4*d3/d4 = 2*4/2 = 4
+      hence 2 < V3=3 <= 4.
+
+i=2:  d2/(n-M2) = 16/12 = 4/3  and V3*d2/d3 = 3*16/4 = 12
+      hence 4/3 < V2=3 <= 12.
+```
+
+Def.5.1(3), using the printed formula recorded in `census-rebase`, gives:
+
+```text
+delta3 = 1 - (n-M3)/(n-M3-1) = 1 - 2/1 = -1.
+
+delta2 = 1 - 12*(3*2-4)/(3*12-4)
+       = 1 - 12*2/32
+       = 1/4.
+
+delta1 = (7t + 2)/(4(3t + 1)).
+```
+
+For `j=2`, `L2=1`, hence `A2=den(delta2)=4`.  With the notation of the
+charged claim:
+
+```text
+P = V3*d2/d3       = 3*16/4 = 12
+Q = V3*(n-M2)/d3   = 3*12/4 = 9
+P = 3*A2 + 0
+triangle = 3, square = 0
+```
+
+Thus `P == 0 mod A2`, so the minimum fixed-zero multiplicity is `b=0`; there
