+
+## 5. Prop.6.3 Descent
+
+Keep separate the two `u` quantities:
+
+```text
+nested-pack budget: u = V3*K/d3 = 12.
+Prop.6.3 top complement: u_s = d_s - V_s = d3 - V3 = 4 - 3 = 1.
+```
+
+Since `u_s=1`, the charged Prop.6.4 automatic hypothesis is met for every
+member of the ray.  The Jacobian exponent is
+
+```text
+v_s - u_s - 1 = 3 - 1 - 1 = 1,
+```
+
+so the descended monomial-Jacobian ray has `J ~ gamma`.
+
+The descended data are:
+
+```text
+n'  = n/d_s  = (48t+16)/4 = 12t+4 = 4(3t+1)
+m'  = m/d_s  = (32t+16)/4 = 8t+4  = 4(2t+1)
+M2' = M2/d_s = (48t+4)/4  = 12t+1
+V2' = 3
+k   = 1
+s'  = 2
+d'  = (d1',d2',d3') = (4(3t+1),4,1)
+```
+
+At `t=1`, this gives
+
+```text
+(n',m',M2',V2',k) = (16,12,13,3,1),
+```
+
+matching Moh p.207's `(16,12; 13; 3; X)` row to the datum.  The independent
+`phi_delta.py` control also prints:
+
+```text
+(16,12) from (64,48): raw=(-1/2, 1/8), Phi=(-1, 1/4),
+printed=(-1, 1/4), MATCH.
+```
+
+For general `t`, Def.5.1(3) on the descended `s'=2` data gives raw radii:
+
+```text
+raw delta2 = -1/2
+raw delta1 = t/(2(3t+1)).
+```
+
+By the Phi rule in the charged helper, `delta' = (k+1)*raw` and `k=1`, hence
+
+```text
+Phi delta2' = -1
+Phi delta1' = t/(3t+1).
+```
+
+The descent anchor does not vanish:
+
+```text
+n' - M2' - 1 = (12t+4) - (12t+1) - 1 = 2.
+```
+
+So `OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]` is closed negatively for this ray: the anchor is
+exactly `2` for all `t >= 1`.
+
+## OPEN Accounting
+
+`OPEN[DESCENT-ANCHOR]` was the only OPEN directly created by this claim.
